# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites files
# to CRLF on checkout. For most files that is harmless. For a few it is fatal:
#
#   - A shell script with CRLF endings has "\r" attached to its shebang, so Linux
#     tries to run the interpreter "/usr/bin/env bash\r", which does not exist.
#     Docker reports this as "no such file or directory" while pointing at a file
#     that is plainly there - one of the more confusing build failures going.
#   - Dockerfiles and YAML are read by Linux tooling that does not expect CR.
#
# Forcing LF on these makes a local Docker build on Windows behave the same as the
# host's build from GitHub.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary - never touch.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
